    {
      "id": "claim_ddcd04f2385a4449bf95c5116b6aafc2",
      "statement": "The set of available sign-in providers is configured at deploy time by the comma-separated environment variable NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_PROVIDERS; getEnabledAuthProviders in lib/auth/providers.ts parses it into a { github, vercel } boolean record that the sign-in UI consumes to decide which buttons to render, with 'github' as the default when the variable is unset.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/auth/providers.ts#L5-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0e0034bda2e6ae30bfbb761db0d87de99e3ebd28b19f238560bd6197f50aa3f5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e533c9493d51496abbd9011861d55ae6",
      "statement": "The two providers use non-symmetric OAuth handshakes: Vercel's sign-in start is POST /api/auth/signin/vercel using arctic's PKCE (S256) flow because arctic has no built-in Vercel adapter, while GitHub's start is GET /api/auth/signin/github using the standard auth-code flow with scopes repo,read:user,user:email and no PKCE; the Vercel callback calls arctic's validateAuthorizationCode against the bespoke endpoint https://vercel.com/api/login/oauth/token.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/auth/callback/vercel/route.ts#L26-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8ed659b769f0563f93092b96f40861ae5b010f7ecf84e663b2cd9285d6b6e7cf:"
        },
        {
