    {
      "id": "claim_2ca2218b61574ccf94238d33811e5a0d",
      "statement": "The sign-in flow uses a dual-cookie model: the long-lived _user_session_ JWE cookie carries identity across requests, while short-lived auxiliary cookies carry provider-specific OAuth state across the redirect. Vercel writes vercel_oauth_state, vercel_oauth_code_verifier, and vercel_oauth_redirect_to (the PKCE verifier being the extra cookie). GitHub writes either github_auth_state + github_auth_redirect_to + github_auth_mode='signin' or github_auth_state + github_auth_redirect_to + github_auth_mode='connect' plus github_oauth_user_id=session.user.id; both callback handlers delete these aux cookies after consuming them, and the GitHub callback still tolerates the legacy github_oauth_* cookie names without an auth_mode cookie.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/auth/callback/vercel/route.ts#L65-L67",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:faeed79d9b32e9a7490b96965f17b3e35eae5367ff13eb9ed35185f76d926387:"
        },
