    {
      "id": "claim_36c6494c231147c48de1dce716026629",
      "statement": "OAuth access tokens are encrypted at rest by lib/crypto.ts using aes-256-cbc with a 16-byte random IV and a 32-byte key from process.env.ENCRYPTION_KEY; encrypt is called from exactly two sites (inside upsertUser for primary tokens and inside the GitHub connect callback for linked-account tokens), and decrypt is the only function that turns stored tokens back into plaintext. The GitHub primary path passes encrypt(accessToken) with refreshToken=undefined because GitHub OAuth does not issue refresh tokens, while the Vercel primary path encrypts both accessToken and refreshToken when present.",
      "evidence": [
