    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d07c005da0024859839ec7a2b8e9d465",
      "statement": "In the GitHub connect flow, app/api/auth/github/callback/route.ts handles three sub-cases: same user re-connecting (in-place token update on the existing accounts row), conflict where another internal user already owns this GitHub identity (transfer tasks, connectors, accounts, and keys from the old user to the connecting user, delete the old users row, and update the existing accounts row to point at the connecting user), and a fresh link (insert a new accounts row with the encrypted token). The conflict sub-case is destructive and irreversible.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/auth/github/callback/route.ts#L142-L210",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8f04e8a3bee0e98831b35bf78ab0f5cf193cb690c9c4b36e79c3ea3383342980:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d995631a349d4a02bf31bfe086f9363b",
      "statement": "/api/auth/signout reads the current session, fetches the upstream token via getOAuthToken, and revokes it at the provider before clearing the cookie: GitHub via DELETE /applications/:client_id/token with HTTP Basic auth, Vercel via POST /api/login/oauth/token/revoke with form-urlencoded body. Revoke failures are logged but never propagated; after revocation the route returns { url } for the client to navigate to and uses saveSession(response, undefined) to emit an immediate-expiry Set-Cookie.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/auth/signout/route.ts#L7-L53",
